cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "COLD READ: The Anonymity Half-Life Is a Property of the Reader"
authors:
  - family-names: "Syed"
    given-names: "Zaid Ali"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4313-1510"
version: 1.4.0
date-released: 2026-10-14
url: "https://github.com/zaidwhy/coldread"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zaidwhy/coldread"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22309660"
abstract: >
  Measures how many words a person must write before a language model
  can infer who they are, with star sign as a negative control that
  never clears its bar. Correction of 2026-11-18 (after v1.4.0): the
  reported 50, 800 and 1600 word gender thresholds were confounded by
  the order of the answer options. With every author asked under both
  orders the three readers clear at 25, 100 and 50 words, and the gap
  between readers appears only when "female" is listed first. See
  RESULT.md step 4 in the repository.
